#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/netutils/wireshark.xml:176
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of Wireshark"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/netutils/wireshark.xml:179
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<application>Wireshark</application> is a very large and complex "
"application. These instructions provide additional security measures to "
"ensure that only trusted users are allowed to view network traffic. First, "
"set up a system group for wireshark.  As the <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/netutils/wireshark.xml:186
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>groupadd -g 62 wireshark</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/netutils/wireshark.xml:189
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Continue to install <application>Wireshark</application> by running the "
"following commands:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/netutils/wireshark.xml:193
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"cmake -D CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr \\\n"
"      -D CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release  \\\n"
"      -D CMAKE_INSTALL_DOCDIR=/usr/share/doc/wireshark-&wireshark-version; \\\n"
"      -G Ninja \\\n"
"      .. &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/netutils/wireshark.xml:204
#, xml-text
msgid "This package does not come with a test suite."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/netutils/wireshark.xml:208
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/netutils/wireshark.xml:211
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>ninja install &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"install -v -m755 -d /usr/share/doc/wireshark-&wireshark-version; &amp;&amp;\n"
"install -v -m644    ../README.linux ../doc/README.* ../doc/randpkt.txt \\\n"
"                    /usr/share/doc/wireshark-&wireshark-version; &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"pushd /usr/share/doc/wireshark-&wireshark-version; &amp;&amp;\n"
"   for FILENAME in ../../wireshark/*.html; do\n"
"      ln -s -v -f $FILENAME .\n"
"   done &amp;&amp;\n"
"popd\n"
"unset FILENAME</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/netutils/wireshark.xml:225
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you downloaded any of the documentation files from the page listed in the"
" 'Additional Downloads', install them by issuing the following commands as "
"the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/netutils/wireshark.xml:232
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>install -v -m644 <replaceable>&lt;Downloaded_Files&gt;</replaceable> \\\n"
"                 /usr/share/doc/wireshark-&wireshark-version;</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/netutils/wireshark.xml:236
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Now, set ownership and permissions of sensitive applications to only allow "
"authorized users.  As the <systemitem class=\"username\">root </systemitem> "
"user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/netutils/wireshark.xml:241
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>chown -v root:wireshark /usr/bin/tshark &amp;&amp;\n"
"chmod -v 6550 /usr/bin/tshark</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/netutils/wireshark.xml:245
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Finally, add any users to the wireshark group (as <systemitem class= "
"\"username\">root</systemitem> user):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/netutils/wireshark.xml:249
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>usermod -a -G wireshark "
"<replaceable>&lt;username&gt;</replaceable></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/netutils/wireshark.xml:252
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you are installing wireshark for the first time, it will be necessary to "
"logout of your session and login again. This will put wireshark in your "
"groups, because otherwise Wireshark will not function properly."
msgstr ""

